From d28248369fb94bbaf2b6874ce202a000edb1f88d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Betterr <51264180+Star-caorui@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:53:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] a2dp: Skip audio context reconfig for SW codecs

Since "a2dp-aidl: Handle source metadata changes", a game sound starting
or stopping makes btif_av reconfigure the current codec with the GAME or
MEDIA audio context. Only codecs configured by the audio HAL provider
use that context. For any other codec, such as the software SBC and AAC
encoders, the reconfiguration changes nothing, but it still ends and
restarts the audio session.

Audio HALs built on the default AIDL implementation disable their
Bluetooth port when the session ends, and enable it again only when the
framework reopens the stream. AudioService does that only when the codec
configuration changed, which is true on the first switch alone, as the
codec priority goes from default to highest. From the second switch on,
everything played over Bluetooth is silent until the headset reconnects.

Skip the reconfiguration when the provider does not support the current
codec. The low latency mode is still recorded and sent to the peer.

Tested on a Redmi Note 13 5G (MediaTek audio HAL) with AAC headphones,
playing media with four switches between game and media usages. Before,
the session restarted on each switch and the port stayed disabled from
the second one on. After, the session was not restarted and the port
stayed started throughout.

Change-Id: I22843348fe6573f69893179f7fd4ec9f03c62c01
---
 system/btif/src/btif_av.cc | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/system/btif/src/btif_av.cc b/system/btif/src/btif_av.cc
index 323af5320c..979442b9df 100644
--- a/system/btif/src/btif_av.cc
+++ b/system/btif/src/btif_av.cc
@@ -2522,6 +2522,12 @@ bool BtifAvStateMachine::StateOpened::ProcessEvent(uint32_t event, void* p_data)
         return false;
       }
 
+      if (!bluetooth::audio::a2dp::provider::supports_codec(current_codec->codecIndex())) {
+        log::info("codec {} does not use the audio context, not reconfiguring",
+                  current_codec->name());
+        break;
+      }
+
       btav_a2dp_codec_config_t codec_config{
               .codec_type = current_codec->codecIndex(),
               .codec_priority = BTAV_A2DP_CODEC_PRIORITY_HIGHEST,
@@ -2795,6 +2801,12 @@ bool BtifAvStateMachine::StateStarted::ProcessEvent(uint32_t event, void* p_data
           return false;
         }
 
+        if (!bluetooth::audio::a2dp::provider::supports_codec(current_codec->codecIndex())) {
+          log::info("codec {} does not use the audio context, not reconfiguring",
+                    current_codec->name());
+          break;
+        }
+
         btav_a2dp_codec_config_t codec_config{
                 .codec_type = current_codec->codecIndex(),
                 .codec_priority = BTAV_A2DP_CODEC_PRIORITY_HIGHEST,
